{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-engineer-cc3-fix-r4.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-11 09:43:02 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 16:43:02 +07\nCoding-Agent: muse\nSession-ID: 32f8fc19-1990-4b12-81b7-c70aed1c1f0c\nModel: muse-wonder-1.0\n\n# cc3 fix round r4 — the three r3-confirm residues (F2/F4/F6): findings\n\nStatus: COMPLETE — all three accepted items fixed and verified in the\nuncommitted eight-file diff on `cc3-lowering-provenance` (base\n`ced9f2c2`; 8 files, +1495/−68 at delivery). Nothing committed. The r4\nchanges touch three of the eight files: `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`\n(F2), `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` + `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`\n(F4); F6 is a corrected measurement + record (script in-repo at\n`collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj`, numbers below and\nin the r3 findings' PREFLIGHT BOUNDS). No forbidden file was edited\n(`macro.cljc`, `ast_walker.cljc`, `semantic.cljc`, `yang/clojure.cljc`,\n`core/prelude.cljc`, `dht.cljc`, `index.cljc` untouched); F1/F3/F5 areas\nwere not touched. Deliverable note: the requested path under\n`/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/` is outside this\nsession's writable workspace (sandbox denied the write, approval\nprompts disabled), so this is the worktree mirror at\n`collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-engineer-cc3-fix-r4.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md`\nin `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3` — copy it to the canonical\ncollab path from a shell with write access there. For the same reason\nthe canonical r3 copy's `F6-NUMBERS-TBD` could not be edited in place;\nsee F6 below.\n\n## Per-finding disposition\n\n### F2 P1 — two origin defects — FIXED\n\n- Batch-token shape ([latte_oracle_test.clj:2456](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2456),\n  origin built at :2481): `kernel-compile`'s scoped arity now builds\n  the admission origin as\n  `(vm/source-origin :program [admission-scope admission-ordinal] 0)` —\n  the token `[run-scope admission-ordinal]` with member index zero, per\n  the reviewer's suggested shape. Projected keys are reconstructed in\n  `cc3-oracle-binding` from a single-member envelope (member index\n  always 0), so projected and searched keys agree for every ordinal,\n  including nonzero ones; the old slot-3 ordinal mismatch is gone.\n- No default admission: the one-argument form (which stamped every\n  admission `[:source :program :oracle-run 0]`) is DELETED. Every\n  caller now supplies explicit coordinates: the principal binding test\n  (`:cc3-binding-run 0`, :3731), the duplicate-ID test\n  (`:cc3-duplicate-run 0`), the proof-supply/proof-loop/check-proof\n  tests (`:proof-fresh-supply`/`:proof-loop`/`:check-proof 0`), and\n  `kernel-row` (`:kernel-row 0`). No hidden global state was added;\n  the coordinate remains composition-supplied plain data validated by\n  `vm/source-origin` when admitting and retained as\n  `:admission-origin`.\n- Test ([latte_oracle_test.clj:3990](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3990)):\n  `test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins` now admits identical\n  content (same canonical hash) under `\"run-a\"` ordinal 0, `\"run-b\"`\n  ordinal 0, and `\"run-a\"` ordinal 1; pins token `[\"run-a\" 1]` and\n  member index 0 for the nonzero ordinal, distinct origins for\n  distinct scopes AND for same-scope/different-ordinal, end-to-end\n  binding under each origin (`cc3-oracle-binding` origin equals the\n  recorded admission origin in all three cases, so binding a nonzero\n  ordinal no longer refuses), distinct bound key sets, and replay\n  stability for `\"run-a\"` ordinal 0.\n\n### F4 P1 — handles lost on link-resume failures — FIXED\n\n- `link-raise` ([repl.cljc:1551](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1551))\n  now carries the interrupted state's `:call-provenance-handles`\n  under `::call-provenance-handles` (merged over any already on the\n  error), alongside the existing link counters/pairs. A claimed\n  program that returns from `run-evaluator-stage` waiting on a\n  query/link has its handles on the state `drive-links` receives;\n  a throw when `drive-links` resumes it (`vm/run` catch, or the\n  query-call-limit raise) therefore carries them out.\n- `run-evaluation` recovery ([repl.cljc:1874](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1874)):\n  a `latest` volatile captures the evaluator stage's result (and the\n  post-`drive-links` state); the catch merges handles from BOTH the\n  error's data and the latest known state into the recovered session\n  — it no longer consults only the pre-evaluator `expanded`. Wedged\n  (non-link) throws after evaluation keep the handles by the same\n  path.\n- `recheck-pending*` recovery likewise merges any\n  `::call-provenance-handles` a link raise carried out of a resumed\n  parked run into the recovered session.\n- Test ([clojure_callsite_test.cljc:2104](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:2104)):\n  `repl-packet-provenance-survives-link-resume-failure-test` (new,\n  JVM lane) evaluates claimed definitions, requires\n  `dao.space.query`, then runs\n  `(let [r (dao.space.query/q (quote [:find (count ?e) . :where [?e :yin/name ?n]]))] (/ 1 0))`\n  — the program parks on the query, is resumed by `drive-links`, and\n  throws `Divide by zero` on resume (observed text `Error: Divide by\n  zero`). Its round's new handle is present in the recovered session\n  and the relation is retrievable by that handle after the durable\n  store is closed and reopened, identical to before reopen.\n\n### F6 P2 — placeholder numbers, flawed measurement — FIXED (record below)\n\nCorrected script in-repo:\n[1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj)\n(byte-identical to the executed `/tmp/cc3-f6-measure-r4.clj`; run\ncommand in the table notes). Corrections, per the reviewer:\n(a) no structure is held by a global Var — everything is built\ninside functions, held only by locals, sampled while provably alive\n(`System/identityHashCode` used after the sample), released on\nreturn, after a discarded warmup build + GC pin; (b) the peak\nsampler (2 ms) spans lowering → binding/projection/derives →\nactual serialization (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`) AND durable\npersistence (`dao.jing/materialize!` of the relation and its record\ninto a file-backed `yin.repl.store`, closed) → tagged execution (both\nC lanes, `:completed`); (c) every `F6-NUMBERS-TBD` in the worktree is\nreplaced with the measured numbers below against the r2-declared\nceilings, method and comparability limits named. The canonical\n(`/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/...`) r3 copy still contains its\n`F6-NUMBERS-TBD` at line 144: this session's sandbox denied writing\noutside the worktree (escalated write refused, approval prompts\ndisabled), so that one replacement is UNVERIFIED/BLOCKED here — the\ntext to substitute is exactly the numbers paragraph in this\nsection. The earlier runs' incomplete-preflight status is preserved\n(r3 PREFLIGHT BOUNDS text untouched; an r4 correction note was\nappended to the worktree r3 copy's PREFLIGHT BOUNDS recording these\nnumbers and noting that a separate 2026-11-11 15:54 edit of that\ncopy recorded a whole-pipeline holder of ~9.18M B, consistent with\nthe compiled-inclusive figure below).\n\n| Quantity | Measured (r4, 2026-11-11, warm JVM) | Declared ceiling (r2, kept) | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Serialized storage: C1 rows (canonical bytes) | 293,924 B | 2,000,000 B per artifact | under |\n| Serialized storage: provenance relation, 3 lanes (canonical bytes) | 802,260 B | 2,000,000 B per artifact | under |\n| Retained JVM memory: `{binding, semantic/stack/register images, relation}`, median of 3 deltas (7,960,192 / 7,921,728 / 8,044,024 B) | 7,960,192 B | 8,000,000 B aggregate session closure | under (99.5%) |\n| Retained JVM memory: same holder plus `compiled`, median of 3 (9,008,912 / 8,939,024 / 8,826,416 B) | 8,939,024 B | 8,000,000 B aggregate session closure | EXCEEDED — measured exceedance recorded, ceiling NOT raised (failure rule) |\n| Peak used heap, 2 ms sampling, lowering → serialization → durable persistence → tagged execution | 292,720,240 B (gc-pinned baseline 38,967,336 B; over-baseline 253,752,904 B) | 1,073,741,824 B (1 GiB) | under |\n| Pipeline elapsed (compile → persistence → both tagged lanes) | 1,727 ms | 10,000 ms | under |\n| Guest instructions / trace records per C lane | restated, NOT raised | 4,000,000 / 1,000,000 (r1) | — |\n\nStage-boundary used-heap samples (same peak run, informational;\nthey fluctuate with GC and are not the ceiling-checked figure):\nafter-compile 64,133,160 B; after-binding 105,278,120 B;\nafter-project-rows 57,582,568 B; after-derives 172,925,928 B;\nafter-serialization 250,007,584 B; after-persistence 89,370,632 B;\nafter-tagged-execution 217,789,448 B. Heap after releasing the\nretained holder returned to 38,966,560 B (baseline 38,967,336 B),\nconfirming the delta tracks the holder's lifetime. Persisted\naddresses (this run): relation\n`:segment/blake3-28ea44a8bcf40bd005ba70e1888cf2ed08063cae62ecf27197707b5cf1994930`,\nrecord\n`:segment/blake3-6a39d41fa2ef2bd252cc1f1055e3223abca4e0c25327439196880ec9c2911840`\n(store since removed with /tmp).\n\nMethod and comparability limits: retained memory and peak are\nprocess-wide JVM used-heap figures (`Runtime.totalMemory −\nfreeMemory`) with `System/gc()` pins, warm JVM after a discarded\nwarmup build. `System/gc()` is a hint the JVM honored observably\nhere, not a guarantee. The retained delta is an\norder-of-magnitude retained-size claim comparable only on this\nhost/JVM and only for the named holder scope — never an exact\nobject-graph census; the two holder scopes above differ by the\ncompiled program and answer differently against the aggregate\nceiling, and a re-scoped ceiling for compiled-inclusive holders is\na landing decision, not this round's (bounds are never silently\nraised). 2 ms peak sampling can miss sub-2 ms transients.\n\n## Red-first evidence\n\nTests were written before the fix for each item; observed red in\nthis session (probe `/tmp/cc3-f4-probe.clj` showed the candidate\nquery-then-divide line returns `Error: Divide by zero` only after\nthe query is served and resumed — the divide is on the resume):\n\n| Item | Red | Green |\n|---|---|---|\n| F2 (oracle) | updated `test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins` (token shape + nonzero ordinal through binding) against the old slot-3 origin: 4 failures, 1 error (ordinal-1 binding refused: projected markers end in `0`, searched keys in `1`) | 0 (4 cc3 oracle tests, 69 assertions) |\n| F4 (durable) | new `repl-packet-provenance-survives-link-resume-failure-test` with both r4 mechanisms disabled (r3 behaviour restored in a scratch toggle): 2 failures (handles 3 before and 3 after the resume-failing round; no retrievable relation) | 0 (7 assertions; fix restored from a byte copy and re-verified in the full battery) |\n| F6 | n/a — measurement/record fix, no code | measured record above; script in-repo |\n\n## Verification\n\n| Lane | Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| Callsite battery | `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 36 tests, 403 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Semantic nets | `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic.linearize-test -n yin.vm.semantic.derive-test` | 51 tests, 7,333 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| REPL nets | `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl-test -n yin.repl.store-test` | 79 tests, 400 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Oracle binding | `… -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-oracle-site-c1-binding` (in the 4-test run) | 0 failures |\n| Oracle nested correspondence | `… -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-stamp-correspondence-nested` | 0 failures |\n| Oracle grammar-data | `… -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-correspondence-verifies-grammar-data` | 0 failures |\n| Oracle distinct admissions (F2) | `… -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins` | 0 failures (4 tests together: 69 assertions) |\n| REPL provenance survives failure (r3) | in callsite battery above | 0 failures |\n| REPL provenance survives link-resume failure (new) | `… -v yang.clojure-callsite-test/repl-packet-provenance-survives-link-resume-failure-test` | 0 failures, 7 assertions |\n| F6 measurement | in-repo script (command in F6 section) | numbers in F6 table; both C lanes `:completed` |\n| kondo (all 8 changed files) | `clj -M:kondo --lint <8 files>` | errors: 0, warnings: 0 |\n\nNote: the combined semantic+repl invocation exceeded this\nlaptop's 280 s command cap in one attempt (exit 124, no failures\nobserved before the cap); it was split by namespace as shown and\nboth halves are green (130 tests, 7,733 assertions in total, as in\nr3). An earlier combined attempt completed with the same suites.\n\n## Invariants and unchanged items\n\n- Zero canonical change, origins never minted, legacy loadable:\n  the F2 coordinate is still supplied by the admitting composition\n  and recorded as plain data; only its slot placement changed\n  (ordinal moved into the batch token, member index fixed at 0 for\n  these single-member admissions). F4 adds no guest instructions;\n  handles remain host-side side artifacts in the content store.\n- No hidden global state: F2 deletes the harness's default\n  admission entirely; every `kernel-compile` caller names its\n  scope/ordinal.\n- F1/F3/F5: untouched (confirmed in r3; this round's oracle run\n  re-verifies F1's deftests).\n- Datom lane and DHT custody: unchanged from the r3 record;\n  `dht.cljc` remains forbidden and unedited.\n\n## Unverified items\n\n- Canonical collab copy of this deliverable and of the r3\n  `F6-NUMBERS-TBD` replacement: write-blocked by this session's\n  sandbox (see F6); the worktree mirrors carry both texts.\n- Full oracle suite and suite-scale battery: shiva at landing (per\n  the original brief); only the four cc3 oracle deftests ran here.\n- cljs/cljd lanes: not run on this laptop; kondo's dual analysis is\n  the evidence (0 errors). The new F4 deftest is JVM-gated\n  (`#?(:clj …)`), consistent with the file-store precedents; the F4\n  fix itself uses only portable `ex-info`/`ex-data`/`volatile!` in\n  `repl.cljc`.\n- Retained-memory method: used-heap delta is an order-of-magnitude\n  claim (see limits above), not an object-graph census; the\n  compiled-inclusive holder exceeds the r2 aggregate ceiling as\n  recorded — a re-scoped ceiling is a landing decision.\n- Cold-JVM time ceilings: declared from warm pilot measurements,\n  as §6.3 permits.\n- The kit contract test: N/A on this laptop (r1 record stands).\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
